        { "text": "<code>\"True\"</code>", "isCorrect": false },
        { "text": "<code>1</code>", "isCorrect": false }
      ],
      "explanation": "Python keywords for boolean values are capitalized. <code>True</code> is the specific keyword representing a boolean true value."
    },
    {
      "questionText": "What is the result of the expression <code>\"10\" + \"20\"</code>?",
      "options": [
        { "text": "<code>30</code>", "isCorrect": false },
        { "text": "<code>\"30\"</code>", "isCorrect": false },
        { "text": "<code>\"1020\"</code>", "isCorrect": true },
        { "text": "Error", "isCorrect": false }
      ],
      "explanation": "When the <code>+</code> operator is used with strings, it performs concatenation (joining). It appends the second string directly to the end of the first."
    },
    {
      "questionText": "What happens if you run <code>x = int(3.9)</code>?",
      "options": [
        { "text": "<code>x</code> becomes <code>4</code>", "isCorrect": false },
        { "text": "<code>x</code> becomes <code>3</code>", "isCorrect": true },
